{# Troubleshooting section #}
<details class="govuk-details govuk-!-margin-top-6">
  <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
    <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
      Troubleshooting: Site not loading
    </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="govuk-details__text">
    <p class="govuk-body">
      If Minute AI does not load:
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>Wait 2 to 3 minutes after stack completion &ndash; CloudFront may need time to propagate</li>
      <li>Check the CloudFormation "Events" tab for any errors</li>
      <li>Try refreshing the page</li>
      <li>Check you are using the correct URL from the Outputs tab</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</details>

<details class="govuk-details">
  <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
    <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
      Troubleshooting: "Session link required" page
    </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="govuk-details__text">
    <p class="govuk-body">
      If you see a page saying <strong>"NDX:Try Minute &ndash; session link required"</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>You opened the <strong>MinuteUrl</strong> instead of the <strong>MinuteLoginUrl</strong>. Go back to the Outputs tab and copy the URL that ends in <code>?key=</code>.</li>
      <li>Some chat clients and email clients strip <code>?key=</code> from links. Copy the URL directly from the CloudFormation Outputs tab, not from a forwarded message.</li>
      <li>If your session has expired (7 days), open the MinuteLoginUrl again to start a new session.</li>
      <li>The 401 page includes a direct link back to the CloudFormation Outputs tab for your stack.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</details>

